      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T10:49:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, thanks. I removed the dependency on `javax.crypto.KDF` and `HKDFParameterSpec`.\n\nThe key derivation now implements HKDF-SHA256 per RFC 5869 using `Mac.getInstance(\"HmacSHA256\")` and `SecretKeySpec`, which is available on the supported Java 21 runtime. I also added an RFC 5869 test vector so the local HKDF implementation is covered directly.",
      "parentUuid": "7668614b_adab3db4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "402fd6c6da5ab0231e09cd9e218966a1aa17a08b",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f87c15f7_3fe4e90f",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/auth/oauth/OAuthTokenAesGcmEncrypter.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T09:18:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comment by Claude:\n\n\u003e  Cipher.getInstance() is relatively expensive (SPI lookup + reflection). For high-traffic deployments, creating a new Cipher on every token read/write will be a performance hotspot. GCM ciphers cannot\n  be safely shared or reused across threads without synchronisation (GCM is stateful), but a ThreadLocal\u003cCipher\u003e pool is a common, safe pattern here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "402fd6c6da5ab0231e09cd9e218966a1aa17a08b",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f6edb6b_351eafb7",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/auth/oauth/OAuthTokenAesGcmEncrypter.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T10:49:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. The code now uses a `ThreadLocal\u003cCipher\u003e`.\n\nThe cipher is still re-initialized for every encrypt/decrypt operation with the derived key, fresh IV for encryption, and the operation-specific AAD. So the stateful GCM cipher is not shared across threads or reused without `init()`.",
      "parentUuid": "f87c15f7_3fe4e90f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "402fd6c6da5ab0231e09cd9e218966a1aa17a08b",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
